     Sprint 37 — Voice Command Brain, Part 1 of 4 (App.VoiceBrain — new)
       App version bumped: 1.31.0 -> 1.32.0
       New module App.VoiceBrain (pure logic, no UI/visual changes).
       Classifies any transcribed voice text into 'navigate' /
       'add_transaction' / 'question' / 'unclear', and routes it to
       the app's real existing handlers instead of guessing:
         - 'navigate' -> the real switchToView(name), for a screen
           list built from the same data-view values already on
           .tab/.more-item elements (new, since nothing previously
           routed voice text to a screen change at all)
         - 'add_transaction' / 'question' -> the real
           App.Chat.open()+sendMessage(text,{viaVoice:true}) — the
           exact call Sprint 19's Bridge already made for every
           transcript, unchanged. App.Chat's own classifyKind() and
           App.OnlineAI fallback (both pre-existing, both untouched)
           still do the actual transaction/question handling and
           follow-up questions
         - 'unclear' (empty/filler input, or a bare screen name with
           no navigation verb) -> needsFollowup:true and nothing is
           dispatched; this is the hook Part 2 builds on
       Checked first, confirmed still placeholders, left untouched:
       App.Voice.Parser.parseCommand(), App.Conversation.Intent.
       detectIntent(), App.Intent.Detector.detectIntent() — all three
       still explicitly log "placeholder, no real classification this
       sprint." None of them were doing real work to reuse.
       Only existing code touched: App.Voice.Bridge.
       handleFinalTranscript() gained one additive branch (App.
       VoiceBrain.handle(text) instead of calling App.Chat directly),
       with the exact pre-Sprint-37 App.Chat call kept as a fallback
       if App.VoiceBrain is ever unavailable. No IDs, classes, event
       listeners, or business logic elsewhere were removed, renamed,
       or altered.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------
     Sprint 36 — More Page Redesign, Step 2 (First 10 Visible Tool Cards)
       App version bumped: 1.31.0 -> 1.32.0
       Visual-only, scoped to the 10 cards currently visible below the
       Sprint 35 hero/featured-action area: AI Assistant, Goals,
       Accounts, Recurring, Categories & Tags, Debts & Loans, Credit
       Cards, Investments, Cash Flow Forecast, Can I Spend This?.
       Each of those 10 .more-item nodes gained one extra class,
       "kh-tool-card" (id/data-view/existing classes untouched), which
       drives: dark glass background (#141B2D), 20px rounded corners,
       soft purple border, a small glowing gradient icon chip behind
       the existing emoji span, larger padding, staggered fade-in,
       hover lift + glow-colour border, an active-state scale press,
       a CSS-only radial "ripple" on click, and a decorative arrow
       (::after, no markup added). No JS, ids, data-view values, or
