     Sprint 25 — Multi-Item Transaction Entry
       App version bumped: 1.22.0 -> 1.23.0
       Mission: let one transaction hold several line items (e.g. a
       single "Food" expense containing Milk/Peanut/Bread/Tea) instead
       of forcing one save per item, while every existing single-item
       transaction, report, chart, budget, goal, and voice/chat flow
       keeps working exactly as before.

       DATA MODEL (additive, backward compatible):
         Every transaction keeps its existing flat shape — id, type,
         date, time, category, subcategory, item, amount, account,
         mode, notes, tags[] — completely unchanged for single-item
         entries (the vast majority of existing data). A NEW optional
         field is added on top: `items[]`, an array of child line
         items ({id, name, amount, qty, unit, notes, tags[]}). When
         `items` is present: the parent's `amount` is always the sum
         of its items' amounts, and `item` becomes a comma-joined
         summary of item names (e.g. "Milk, Peanut, Bread, Tea") — so
         every existing reader of `t.amount`/`t.category`/`t.item`
         (reports, budgets, goals, analytics, search, CSV export,
         dashboards) keeps summing/filtering/displaying correctly with
         ZERO changes, while a new `isMultiItem` flag and the `items`
         array itself let new UI show/edit the breakdown. Transactions
         without `items` are indistinguishable from pre-Sprint-25 data.
         New shared helper: App.Transaction.MultiItem (Config-free
         utility: cleanItem/sum/summaryLabel/buildParentTxn/addItem/
         removeItem/duplicateItem/moveItem) — the ONE place that knows
         how to turn a list of items into a valid parent transaction.
         Reused by all three entry points below instead of duplicating
         the math three times.

       MANUAL ENTRY (New Transaction form, App.Attachments/App.OCR
       untouched):
         A new "🧾 Add multiple items" toggle under the existing
         Item/Description field reveals an item repeater (name +
         amount per row, with a collapsible "⋯" for optional qty/unit/
         notes) plus a live running total. Add Item / Delete Item /
         Duplicate Item / Reorder (↑↓) all work on this in-memory list
         before save. The existing single Amount + Item/Description
         fields, and the entire Income/Transfer flow, are completely
         unchanged and remain the default — multi-item is strictly
         opt-in per transaction. On submit, if multi-item mode has at
         least one valid row, App.Transaction.MultiItem.buildParentTxn
         builds the parent transaction the same way saveDraft() (chat/
         voice) and the Items Editor (below) do; otherwise the
         pre-Sprint-25 single-item save path runs byte-for-byte as
         before.

       EDITING EXISTING TRANSACTIONS:
         The existing pencil-icon amount-only edit prompt is untouched
         (still works exactly as before for every transaction). A new
         "🧾 N" badge appears only on transactions that already have
         `items` — tapping it expands an inline item breakdown in the
         Transactions list/cards (the REPORTS requirement: totals stay
         correct, but child items are viewable), with an "Edit items"
         link that opens a new bottom sheet (App.Transaction.
         ItemsEditor, same .sheet-overlay pattern as the existing
         Attachments manager) supporting Add/Delete/Edit/Reorder/
         Duplicate on that transaction's items, recomputing the parent
         amount/item summary on save via the same buildParentTxn().

       VOICE / CHAT (App.Chat — the live engine behind both typed chat
       and App.Voice.Bridge; App.Conversation/App.Intent remain the
       untouched architecture-only placeholders they already were):
         Purely additive extension of the existing slot-filling
         session for kind==='expense'. Two new regex helpers,
         parseItemAmountSegment()/extractItemAmountPairs(), recognize
         "<item> <amount>" phrases (e.g. "Milk 60", "₹120 for Peanut"),
         reused from both the initial message and every follow-up
         while items are being collected. A new 'moreItems' slot-
         filling step collects items one at a time ("Milk 60." →
         "Peanut 120." → "Bread 40." → "Tea 20." → "Save.") before
         falling through to the existing account/confirmation steps,
         then saveDraft() calls the same buildParentTxn() as the other
         two entry points. A bare number with no item name (e.g. just
         "150") is never matched by the item regex, so every existing
         single-amount voice/chat flow — and every non-expense kind —
         is completely unaffected.

       NOT in this sprint (disclosed rather than silently skipped):
       per-item file attachments — App.Attachments is keyed one-per-
       transaction, so a scanned receipt still attaches at the parent
       transaction level and covers all its items, exactly as before.

