     KHAATA — BUILD LOG
     Sprint 23 — Business Foundation (App.Business — new)
       App version bumped: 1.20.0 -> 1.21.0
       Mission: lay the foundation that every future Business module
       (Customers, Vendors, Products, Inventory, Invoices, Payments,
       Accounting, Reports, GST/Tax, Cloud Sync — none of them exist
       yet) will build on, so the same app can eventually serve
       Personal users, Families, Freelancers, Shop Owners, Small
       Businesses and Accountants without forking into separate apps.
       THIS SPRINT ONLY BUILDS THE FOUNDATION — no Customers, Vendors,
       Products, Inventory, Invoices, Payments, GST, Tax or Cloud Sync
       were implemented, exactly as scoped.
       IMPORTANT — reuse, not duplication: every existing save*()
       function (saveTransactions, saveBudgets, saveAccounts, ...) and
       loadState() itself are the ONLY things touched, and only in one
       mechanical way — the hardcoded 'khaata:xxx' localStorage key
       string each one already used is now resolved through one new
       tiny helper, bizKey('xxx'), instead of being typed inline.
       bizKey() lives right next to uid()/todayStr() (existing helpers)
       and falls back to the exact original 'khaata:xxx' key whenever
       App.Business hasn't loaded yet, so nothing about a single-
       profile ("Personal") session changes: same functions, same
       signatures, same keys, same call sites, same behavior. No new
       parallel saveBusinessTransactions()-style functions were
       written anywhere — that would have been duplication.
         App.Business.Config     profile constants, the list of 21
                               state fields that get isolated per
                               profile (transactions, budgets,
                               budgetTypes, customSubcats, goals,
                               settings, accounts, recurring, debts,
                               tags, creditCards, ccUtilHistory,
                               investments, investmentWatchlist,
                               investmentHistory, netWorthHistory,
                               voiceSettings, voiceLog, reminders,
                               advisor, custom expense/income cats)
         App.Business.Logger     scoped logging, delegates to the
                               existing App.Logger — same pattern
                               App.Voice.Logger/App.Advisor.Logger
                               already use
         App.Business.Storage    resolveKey(base) — the single place
                               that decides whether a key resolves to
                               the plain 'khaata:base' (Personal) or
                               'khaata:biz:<id>:base' (a Business
                               profile); resetScopedState() — blanks
                               the 21 isolated state fields back to
                               their defaults before a switch loads a
                               different profile's data over them
         App.Business.Profile    list/create/rename/remove for
                               Business profiles (Personal is a fixed,
                               un-removable, un-renamable entry that
                               isn't stored — it just always exists).
                               Future-ready: any number of Business
                               profiles, not just one
         App.Business.Session    tracks + persists which profile is
                               active ("khaata:business:active"),
                               restored the moment the script parses
                               — before loadState() ever runs — so
                               loadState() hydrates the correct
                               profile's data on the very first load,
                               no "load Personal then swap" step
         App.Business.Workspace  thin facade (activeProfileId(),
                               activeProfile(), isBusinessProfile(),
                               scopedKey()) that future Business
                               modules (Customers, Vendors, Invoices,
                               ...) will read instead of re-inventing
                               profile isolation themselves
         App.Business.Security   name sanitization + guard rails
                               (Personal can never be renamed/removed)
         App.Business.Manager    switchProfile() — the actual instant
                               switch: reset the 21 isolated fields →
                               point Session at the target profile →
                               call the existing loadState() again
                               (100% reused, not reimplemented) → re-
                               run the same populate*/render*
                               functions App.init() already calls to
                               refresh every visible tab. Also renders
                               and binds the new profile switcher.
       Data isolation — what's fully separated per profile now:
       Transactions, Budgets (both the original budgets{} map and the
       Sprint-21 budgetTypes[]), Goals, Accounts, Recurring, Debts,
       Tags, Credit Cards (+ utilization history), Investments (+
       watchlist + history), Net Worth History, Reminders, the
       Advisor's personalization state, Voice Settings, Voice Log,
       custom categories/subcategories, and the buffer-months setting.
       Since the existing Dashboard/Reports/Insights/Advisor/Budget/
       Goals tabs already compute everything live from these same
       state fields (see their own Sprint 13/14/20/21/22 build-log
       entries — none of that math was ever cached across a whole
       session), they become correctly per-profile for free the
       moment the underlying state is isolated — nothing in App.
       Dashboard/App.Reports/App.Advisor/App.Budget/App.Goals/App.
       Investment was touched.
       Known, deliberate limits of this foundation (by design, not
       oversight): (1) Theme stays global/shared across profiles —
       it's a device display preference, not business data, and
       flipping it on every switch would look like the UI redesigning
       itself, which rule 6 forbids. (2) App.Memory (AI chat memory,
       IndexedDB "khaataMemory") and App.Attachments (receipt images,
       IndexedDB "khaata_attachments_db") still use one shared
       database across all profiles — real per-profile isolation for
       those needs edits inside their own closures (DB_NAME is a
       private const in each IIFE) and was judged too high-risk to
       rush into a "foundation only" sprint; flagged here explicitly
       so Sprint 24+ can pick it up deliberately instead of it being
       silently forgotten. (3) Removing a Business profile from the
       switcher does not delete its stored data — a safety choice so
       a mis-click can never wipe a business's books; real deletion
       (with confirmation) is left for later.
       New UI: one small <select id="businessProfileSwitcher"> added
       to the existing topbar-actions, next to the theme toggle —
       lists Personal + every Business profile plus "＋ New
       Business…". No existing tab, button, form, or layout was
       redesigned, reordered, or removed.
       New storage keys: "khaata:business:profiles" (the Business
       profile list), "khaata:business:active" (last active profile
       id) — both new, additive, same localStorage the app already
       uses. Every existing "khaata:xxx" key keeps meaning exactly
       what it always meant when Personal is active (bizKey() resolves
       to the identical literal), so old data opens exactly as before.
       Regression check result: PASS. Traced every call site of the
       ~20 edited save*() functions and loadState() — none had their
       signature, return type, or call site changed, so every existing
       caller (transaction save, budget save, account save, the
       import/export + Google Drive backup flow, migrateToV2(), etc.)
       keeps working unmodified. migrateToV2() itself needed no
       changes: its internal saveTransactions()/saveAccounts()/
       saveRecurring()/saveBudgets()/saveCustomCats() calls now
       correctly write back to whichever profile is active, instead
       of (bug, caught before shipping) always writing to Personal's
       plain keys regardless of the active profile.
       Compatibility status: 100% backward compatible. A user who
       never touches the new profile switcher sees zero behavior
       change — same keys, same functions, same data, same UI, same
       version bump only in App.Config.VERSION.
       Modules added: App.Business.Config/Logger/Storage/Profile/
       Session/Workspace/Security/Manager (8 sub-modules, all new).
       Ready for Sprint 24.
     ================================================================== -->
