     KHAATA — BUILD LOG
     Sprint 20 — Personal AI Financial Advisor (App.Advisor — new)
       App version bumped: 1.16.0 -> 1.18.0
       (Note: the Sprint 19 entry below says "1.16.0 -> 1.17.0", but the
       App.Config.VERSION constant in the code was still 1.16.0 at the
       start of this sprint — a pre-existing mismatch between that log
       entry and the actual code, not something this sprint introduced.
       Bumped to 1.18.0, not 1.17.0, so the number is unambiguous either
       way this file's history gets read.)
       Mission: turn the app into a proactive Personal AI Financial
       Advisor rather than waiting for the user to open a tab. This
       sprint adds exactly one new top-level namespace, App.Advisor, and
       one new tab ("AI Advisor", id="view-advisor").
       IMPORTANT — reuse, not duplication: the app already computes a
       weighted Financial Health Score (computeHealthScoreDetail — 6
       areas: savings, budget, emergency fund, debt, credit, goals),
       spending-anomaly detection (anomalyAlerts), a spending forecast
       (spendingPrediction), an emergency-fund goal/target
       (getEmergencyFundGoal + the Goals engine's computeGoalPlan /
       computeGoalStatus), and all of this already powers the existing
       "Insights" and "AI Reports" tabs. App.Advisor does NOT recompute
       any of that — App.Advisor.Manager and its sub-modules call those
       exact functions directly. What's new in App.Advisor is only what
       didn't exist anywhere in the app before this sprint:
         App.Advisor.Config          thresholds (offline, no tuning UI)
         App.Advisor.Logger          personalization memory — records
                               which recommendations were shown/
                               dismissed (state.advisor, new storage key
                               "khaata:advisor") so a dismissed
                               suggestion is hidden for a 14-day
                               cooldown instead of repeating every run
         App.Advisor.Analysis        daily/monthly/yearly income,
                               expense, savings, cash-flow, investment
                               and loan pattern rollups — new
                               aggregation built from the app's existing
                               expenseTxns/incomeTxns/sum/monthsRange
                               primitives
         App.Advisor.Budget          budget-usage suggestions: over/near
                               limit, big un-budgeted categories,
                               budgets consistently under 50% used
         App.Advisor.Savings         subscription detection — both
                               what's already declared in Recurring,
                               and untracked repeat charges (same
                               item+category+~amount for 2+ consecutive
                               recent months) — plus the emergency-fund
                               gap, reusing getEmergencyFundGoal()
         App.Advisor.Goals           goal-pace nudges, wraps the
                               existing computeGoalPlan/computeGoalStatus
         App.Advisor.Risk            loan repayment priority (avalanche
                               order — highest interest first) and a
                               conservative, rule-based investment-
                               readiness score/level — both new, no
                               guaranteed-return claims, consistent with
                               the app's existing no-investment-advice
                               stance
         App.Advisor.Notifications   real-time save-time checks — new.
                               Hooked into the existing #txnForm submit
                               handler right after its unchanged
                               saveTransactions() call: duplicate-
                               looking entry, abnormal amount vs. the
                               category's own recent average, budget
                               overspend, low account balance. Shows a
                               small toast (.advisor-toast, new CSS
                               reusing existing color tokens) — never
                               blocks or delays the save itself
         App.Advisor.Recommendations aggregates Budget/Savings/Goals/
                               Risk output, filters out anything
                               dismissed within its cooldown, dedupes,
                               sorts by priority — new
         App.Advisor.Manager         run()/getSnapshot()/init() —
                               caches the last run in
                               state.advisor.snapshot so the tab renders
                               instantly; wired into App.init() the same
                               way every other module's Manager.init()
                               already is
         App.Advisor.UI               render() for the new tab
       New tab ("AI Advisor", id="view-advisor") added to the top tab
       bar and the "More" sheet only (not the 5-item bottom nav, to
       avoid changing that layout) — additive, does not touch the
       existing "Insights", "AI Reports", "Monthly Report", "Budgets",
       or "Goals" tabs, all of which render exactly as they did before.
       New storage key: "khaata:advisor" (dismissed suggestions, shown
       log, last-run cache) — added to App.Storage the same way every
       other save*() function already is; no existing storage key,
       schema, or save*() function was changed.
       No paid APIs, no network calls — same offline-first rule as
